cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Omega-S in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Omega-S: A Functional Resilience Index for LLM Fine-Tuning"
abstract: >
  Omega-S is a regularizer for large-scale neural networks (topological by
  construction, degree-variance-controlling as measured) that penalizes
  structural monopolies in weight connectivity graphs via Hutchinson trace
  estimation of Tr(A³) on the weight adjacency matrix A = WW⊤. It needs no
  previous-task data, no Fisher matrix and no stored copy of the old weights.
  On Llama-3-8B with LoRA it retains more of the original capability than no
  regularisation on 9 of 10 seeds, and adds under 0.4% to the cost of a
  training step.
